2f:T1041,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I book a private transfer in Madinah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Send your pickup, drop-off, date, passengers and luggage by the form or on WhatsApp. We reply with the vehicle and one fixed fare before anything is booked — no meter and no surge. Cancellation is free up to 24 hours before pickup."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is Madinah Airport (MED) from central Madinah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prince Mohammad bin Abdulaziz International Airport (MED) is about 20 km from the Central Area, ~25 min on a clear road. Traffic near Masjid an-Nabawi at prayer times can add to that. We track your flight and the first 15–30 minutes of waiting is free."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the driver take me to the door of my hotel near Masjid an-Nabawi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The driver takes you as close as vehicles are permitted. Access around Al-Masjid an-Nabawi is restricted and varies with prayer times, so the driver uses the nearest permitted drop-off point to your hotel and tells you where to meet for the return."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you offer Madinah Ziyarat by car?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A private car takes you between the sites you choose — such as Quba Mosque, Masjid al-Qiblatayn, the Seven Mosques area and Mount Uhud — and waits at each stop. We provide transport only, not a guide or religious guidance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book a private driver in Madinah for several hours?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Book a car and driver for a block of hours or a full day; the car waits between stops. Send your date, start time and hours needed and we confirm the fare before booking. A single transfer is simpler when you only have one or two stops."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you take me from Madinah to Makkah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Madinah to Makkah is about 430 km and ~4 hr of driving, hotel to hotel, with prayer and rest stops on request. The return trip can be booked at the same time, and Makkah to Madinah runs the other way."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I stop at Dhul Hulayfah (Abyar Ali) on the way to Makkah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Ask for a stop at Dhul Hulayfah when you book a Madinah to Makkah transfer and we confirm it as part of the quote. Whether to enter ihram there is a personal religious matter we cannot advise on — please ask a qualified scholar."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you take me from Madinah to Jeddah Airport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Madinah to King Abdulaziz International Airport (JED) is about 410 km, ~3 hr 50 min. We work the pickup back from your flight time. The reverse, Jeddah Airport to Madinah, is also available and we track your flight."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you take me from Madinah to AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Madinah to AlUla is about 330 km, roughly ~3 hr by road. A private car goes door to door to your AlUla hotel or the airport, and AlUla to Madinah is booked the same way."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can families travel with luggage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A sedan fits one to three people with normal luggage. A GMC or full-size SUV, or a Hyundai Staria, suits families with more luggage. A Hiace van or coaster suits larger groups. Tell us passengers and large bags and we confirm the vehicle when we quote."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is a private transfer in Madinah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the route, the vehicle and the time. We do not publish fixed price lists because they would not be accurate: you send the trip and we confirm one fixed fare on WhatsApp before booking. There is no meter and no surge pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do the drivers speak English?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Drivers in our partner network speak English and Arabic, and trips run 24 hours a day."}}]}29:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2f"}}]
